  "units": "m",
  "description": "A simple illustrated journey introduces scalar length and vector position for page 38, topic 2.3. A blue dashed path around a pond is exactly 120 m long; a coral arrow from the start to the finish is 20 m north. One action follows the path, then reveals the straight position arrow with clear Bangla labels. Three short comparisons show only two of the book’s A/B/C/D vectors at a time: equal magnitude and direction, changed direction, changed magnitude. One action, result and rule; five tap-answer questions; keyboard access, offline operation and six responsive layouts. Distances are to scale; trees and pond are symbolic.",
